Mechanical-engineering sources — complete readings and primary methods (@mech-sources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering) { r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2
Begin with the complete statics book and the Slocum design companion. The dynamics course, mathematics lessons and Tong notes develop moving systems; later sources connect material behavior, machine elements, constraints and joints. Follow each source's actual edition, passages and access notes. All books, PDFs, spreadsheets, media and software remain external references. Roylance and Bower connect observed material behavior to structural models, experiments and advanced numerical methods. SKF’s catalogue and maintenance handbook connect selection with physical assembly and service evidence; their free-reading access differs from the open licences of some teaching sources.

